From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:15:07 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 24/42] docs/system/arm/chumby-classic: Document the USB host

List the USB host controller among the emulated devices, drop the
transfer engine from the missing ones, and show how to attach a USB
stick and keyboard. The stock root disk mounts a stick's first
partition on /mnt/usb.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
 docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst b/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
index 017260afd..1faab49c4 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@ Emulated devices:
 - LCD controller: background plane and graphic window, 16 bpp
 - NAND flash controller with a 64 MiB small-page NAND chip
 - PWM, driving the LCD backlight: the screen is dimmed by its duty cycle
-- USB host's root hub (no devices)
+- USB host controller with a three-port full-speed root hub: control,
+  bulk, interrupt and isochronous transfers, so QEMU's USB devices
+  (``usb-storage``, ``usb-kbd``, ``usb-mouse``, ``usb-tablet``,
+  ``usb-audio``, ``usb-hub``...) can be plugged in with ``-device``
 - DMA controller: 16 channels, linear, 2D and FIFO transfers, repeat
   (chaining) and the bus error status; the timeouts are not modelled
 - SSI1 and SSI2 (as slaves of the codec, in normal, network and I2S
@@ -34,8 +37,10 @@ Emulated devices:
 
 Missing devices:
 
-- Watchdog, RTC, SDHC, I2C and the USB transfer
-  engine: their registers read back what was last written
+- Watchdog, RTC, SDHC and I2C: their registers read back what was
+  last written
+- The USB OTG block's function (device) side, HNP and its transceiver
+  I2C master
 
 Boot options
 ------------
@@ -67,6 +72,15 @@ can also be driven from QMP with ``input-send-event`` (``abs`` events on
 the ``x`` and ``y`` axes, 0 to 32767 across the screen, and the ``left``
 button). ``screendump`` captures the screen.
 
+USB devices attach to the host controller's root hub, for example a
+disk image as a USB stick and a keyboard::
+
+  -drive if=none,id=stick,file=stick.img,format=raw \
+  -device usb-storage,drive=stick -device usb-kbd
+
+The stock root disk mounts the first partition of a stick, ``sda1``, on
+``/mnt/usb``.
+
 The top button (the "squeeze switch", ``/dev/switch`` in the guest) is the
 machine's ``button`` property: ``qom-set /machine button true`` presses
 it and ``qom-set /machine button false`` releases it. A key also holds it
